.TH "RTCTRANSPORTSTATS.ICELOCALUSERNAMEFRAGMENT" "3JS" "June 20, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCTransportStats.iceLocalUsernameFragment \- RTCTransportStats:
iceLocalUsernameFragment property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]iceLocalUsernameFragment\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]RTCTransportStats\f[R] dictionary is a string that indicates the
local username fragment (\(lqufrag\(rq or \(lqice\-ufrag\(rq) that
uniquely identifies the ICE interaction session managed by this
transport.
.PP
The same username fragment is used to identify the session for any
communication with the STUN server.
.PP
This has the same values as the corresponding local
\f[CR]RTCIceCandidate.usernameFragment\f[R] property.
It will change if the connection is renegotiated, for example on ICE
restart, or if \f[CR]RTCPeerConnection.setLocalDescription()\f[R] is
called.
.SH VALUE
A string containing the username fragment that uniquely identifies the
ongoing ICE session on the transport.
.PP
The string may be up to 256 characters long, and has no default value.
